 improving move, the first move (i, j) in row-major order on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ties, until no exchange of two tour edges for two lighter ones remains. The first vertex of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tour"},{"type":"text","text":" stays first. Only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tour.vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" is read: the result uses the lightest edge of each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pair, as every tour does. nil below three vertices."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A move’s gain is formed as (d(a, b) + d(c, e)) − (d(a, c) + d(b, e)), and the scan stops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when no move gains anything. With floating-point weights, rounding decides which moves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gain."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is complete; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tour.vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" lists every vertex of the graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly once; no weight is NaN or infinite; the sum of any two weights fits in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n²) per improving move."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tour"},{"type":"text","text":" improved by 2-opt to a 2-optimal tour."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Edges-swift.associatedtype":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","text":"Collection"}],"t